# Superpowers working scratch — never committed.
# plans/ and specs/ are drafting output; their durable content is redirected into
# backlog/ instead (execution plans -> the task's ## Implementation Plan; design
# specs -> a backlog/decisions/ record or the task description). See CLAUDE.md §Workflow.
docs/superpowers/

# Kotlin build tooling session data
.kotlin/

# Git worktrees (owner convention: .worktree/<branch-name>)
.worktree/
# Agent worktrees, created by the harness per subagent. Not ignoring these lets a
# `git add -A` commit them as gitlinks, which is how three landed in a commit once.
.claude/worktrees/

# Captured device session prefs — these hold real Plex tokens. plex-session.sh keeps its
# backup in $HOME by default; these rules exist so a copy made inside the repo by mistake
# cannot be committed.
ChronicleAuth.xml
Chronicle.xml
chronicle_debug.xml
.chronicle-session-backup/
